From b92bd2a996e930ce5de37b2dfa6b94bb154b96de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chaton <definitelyfrenchname@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 15:24:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cps2w: vsavjw catalogue CRCs for the M17 pyron-capture freeze

jtframe's .rom builder resolves zip members by CRC32 and by nothing else, so
the catalogue entry has to name the CRCs of the actual build. merged-m17
(build/m3b_merged25) moves four members against merged-m16:

    vsw.33m  4d63bfae -> 263cb145
    vsw.37m  9df9677f -> 2a70f185

(the two group-C glyph members, the M16 -> M17 mark) and the program members
carrying Pyron's capture row 0x11 port.

Generated by tools/gen_vsavjw_xml.py from build/m3b_merged25's vsavjw.zip
with the pristine vsav.zip as parent; no other member, count or attribute
changed. Upstream cores/cps1, cores/cps2 and cores/cps15 remain byte-untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Pt4MJ8HCFjymqExvUoiDEc
